---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Making school outreach easier to teach | Morgan Escott">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="text-gray underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/#projects">← All projects</a>

    <header class="case-heading mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-6 md:p-10">
      <p class="text-sm text-white/80">Treering · Sales enablement</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-heading text-white md:text-6xl">Making school outreach easier to teach</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/90">
        A rep could know exactly what they wanted to say to a school and still need help finding
        the right email sequence. At Treering, part of my job was getting that knowledge out of
        my head and into tools the whole team could use.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="case-copy mt-10 space-y-9">
      <section>
        <h2>Start with the reader</h2>
        <p>For a yearlong email series, I segmented messages by school level and the reader’s role.
          That distinction mattered when a rep sat down to write. Knowing a contact worked at a school
          was only a starting point. Which part of the yearbook did that person actually handle?</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Make the work findable</h2>
        <p>I reorganized 129 existing Outreach sequences, added tags, and documented how to use the
          library. I also created a 14-category campaign QA checklist so reviewing a campaign before
          launch was a process a teammate could repeat.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Give new reps somewhere to look</h2>
        <p>I built an internal onboarding site that walked through browser setup, Salesforce tags,
          and outbound workflows, with diagrams and team resources. It became part of formal
          onboarding. I trained more than 20 teammates on Salesforce and Outreach, and the guide
          gave people somewhere to return to after a workshop.</p>
      </section>
      <a class="inline-block text-white underline underline-offset-4" href="https://moreganooooo.github.io/CuripodApplication/#stories">Read my original field stories →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-heading {
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at top right, #82502d75, transparent 65%),
      linear-gradient(125deg, #281334, #58213e);
  }
  .case-copy h2 {
    color: white;
    font: 1.65rem/1.25 var(--font-heading);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .case-copy p {
    color: #ffffffcf;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
</style>
